  "verdict": "The corpus 3D-index engine on SnapPy's triangulations reproduces GGM's printed Ind^rot_{5_2}(0,1;q) = 1-12q+3q^2+74q^3+90q^4 (eq 102) exactly, and the DGG 4_1 index; the (-2,3,7) rotated-index family Ind^rot(m,zeta;q), m=-2..2, is now DERIVED to q^3 (exact integers). By GGM Conjecture 4 this family determines the pretzel's Stokes matrix S^+(x;q) up to GL(r, Z(x,q)) and gives S^+_{sigma1 sigma1}(x;q) exactly; the printed q->0 integer matrices (the {3,4} of 4_1/5_2) sit in GGM's holomorphic-block normalisation, which the pretzel lacks in print, so qou-m3ad item 1 ('are the Stokes entries built from s(x)?') cannot be run AS POSED — it is not GL-invariant. Recorded: at order q^1 the m=0 coefficients are -(s-1)(s+1), -s(s+1), -2(s+1) for 4_1, 5_2, (-2,3,7) — a common factor (s+1) — and at q^2 the 4_1 coefficient is -s^2, so that factor is not universal. A basis-invariant restatement of H_Ad is the open piece.",
